   "text": "I read the structure as a linear peptide with one disulfide-bridged macrocycle (two penicillamine residues) and a lipidated Lys side chain. I assigned stereochemistry by assuming L-configuration at every \u03b1-carbon. I did not read wedges or hashes at each centre, so some centres may be wrong, particularly the Lys that carries the PEG\u2013diacid chain and the trimethylammonium-bearing carbon.\n\n**Sequence, from the C-terminal Gly-NH2 end:**\n1. The C-terminus is a primary amide, H2N\u2013C(=O)\u2013CH2\u2013N(CH3), i.e. N-methylglycinamide.\n2. Next come 3-pyridylalanine, Asn, Glu (free side-chain acid) and 4-aminotetrahydropyran-4-carboxylic acid.\n3. Then 2-naphthylalanine and Tyr, with its phenol O-alkylated as OCH2CH2NH2.\n4. Pen1 begins the ring, followed by Lys(NHAc), 7-methyl-Trp, Thr and Asn.\n5. Pen2 closes the ring. The two penicillamine S atoms are joined by a disulfide (ring label %10).\n\n**Lys side chain on Pen2's N-terminal neighbour:**\n- The \u03b1-amine carries two OCH2CH2OCH2CH2NH\u2013C(=O)CH2 (PEG-type) units in series. These lead to a \u03b3-Glu whose \u03b1-NH is acylated by an 18-carbon diacid (C(=O) + 16 CH2 + COOH). I counted the diacid chain length from the zigzag spacing in the drawing.\n- The \u03b5-amine carries a succinyl group. This links to an Asp-like unit whose side chain is CH2COOH and whose other arm is CH2\u2013N\u207a(CH3)3.\n\nSMILES: NC(=O)CN(C)C(=O)[C@H](Cc1cccnc1)NC(=O)[C@H](CC(N)=O)NC(=O)[C@H](CCC(=O)O)NC(=O)C1(CCOCC1)NC(=O)[C@H](Cc1ccc2ccccc2c1)NC(=O)[C@H](Cc1ccc(OCCN)cc1)NC(=O)[C@H](C(C)(C)S%10)NC(=O)[C@H](CCCCNC(C)=O)NC(=O)[C@H](Cc1c[nH]c2c(C)cccc12)NC(=O)[C@H]([C@@H](C)O)NC(=O)[C@H](CC(N)=O)NC(=O)[C@H](C(C)(C)S%10)NC(=O)[C@H](CCCCNC(=O)CCC(=O)N[C@H](CC(=O)O)C[N+](C)(C)C)NC(=O)COCCOCCNC(=O)COCCOCCNC(=O)CC[C@H](NC(=O)CCCCCCCCCCCCCCCCC(=O)O)C(=O)O"
